1 teaspoon whole cumin or whole black mustard seed
1 tablespoon ground corriander
1/4 to 1/2 teaspoon ground turmeric
1 teaspoon salt
1 tablespoon mango powder
any combination of 1 tablespoon each of minced garlic and or 1 tablespoon ginger and or 1-3 minced serano peppers (optional)
1 medium onion, chopped
1 to 1 1/2 pounds chopped vegetable
1/4 to 1/2 cup celantro chopped with stems (optional)


1) Heat oil and pan on medium high.

2) Add the cumin or black mustard seed to the hot oil. If mustard seed immediately cover with a lid and wait until the sputtering subsides to continue with the next step.

3) Add any of garlic, ginger, and serano peppers if using. Stir for about 30 seconds.

4) Add one chopped onion if using. Stir 5-7 minutes until it's starting to get translucent.

5) Add 1 to 1 1/2 pounds chopped vegetable. Add corriander, turmeric, and salt. Stir until the vegetable is almost done.

6) One minute from the vegetable being done, add and stir in 1 TBSP mango powder and celantro if using.

7) It's ready to serve. :-)
